<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mstislav Mstislavich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1228</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Mstislav the Bold, Mstislav Udatny</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mstislav Mstislavich, called the Bold (Udatny), was a Rus' prince who ruled Novgorod at intervals from 1210 to 1217 and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>. Allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstantin-of-rostov">Konstantin of Rostov</a>, he defeated Yuri and Yaroslav of Vladimir at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lipitsa">Battle of Lipitsa</a> in 1216. He was among the princes defeated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-kalka-river">Battle of the Kalka River</a> in 1223, and died in 1228.</p></div>
